      "reply": "You're all set for Rouen! Here's a quick recap and your deliverables.\n\n**Summary of deliverables:**\n1. **Plan/comparison** \u2014 `Rouen-Neighbourhood-Comparison.md`: Mont-Saint-Aignan, Rouen Centre, and Bois-Guillaume compared on rent, commute, safety and amenities, with a clear recommendation (Mont-Saint-Aignan first choice, Rouen Centre as a lively second option) and a shortlisting checklist.\n2. **Message** \u2014 `Email-to-Landlords-FR-EN.md`: a ready-to-send French rental application email (with an English reference version below), mentioning your NEOMA status, arrival date, and personal guarantor \u2014 just fill in the brackets.\n3. **Image** \u2014 `Rouen-Move-In-Checklist-Poster.png`: a one-page printable checklist covering first steps, accommodation, and daily-life admin.\n4. **Calendar events** (created, Google Calendar):\n   - 4 Jan 2027 \u2014 Move-in day / home insurance must be active\n   - 10 Jan 2027 \u2014 Apply for CAF housing aid (APL)\n   - 11 Jan 2027 \u2014 Open a French bank account\n   - 4 Apr 2027 \u2014 Deadline: validate VLS-TS visa with OFII\n\nA couple of things to keep in mind: rents shift week to week, so re-check listings close to your move-in date, and no official crime dataset exists for Mont-Saint-Aignan or Rouen Centre, so treat safety comments there as general impressions, not statistics. Bon courage for the move \u2014 you've got a solid head start! <cite url=\"https://www.service-public.fr/particuliers/vosdroits/F16162\"/> <cite url=\"https://www.caf.fr/allocataires/caf-de-paris/actualites-departementales/tout-savoir-sur-l-aide-au-logement-etudiant\"/> <cite url=\"https://www.service-public.fr/particuliers/vosdroits/F31300\"/>",
